From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hermes <hermes@local>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:54:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] host: DM_HLECOUNT writes the table while the game runs, not
 only on the way out

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: DM_HLECOUNT writes its table on the way out, and the way out the player actually uses is a swipe from the app
 switcher, which kills the process before atexit runs: the file never appeared, so the switch was unusable exactly
 where it was needed. Writing the same table with the 300-frame readouts costs one small file every five seconds and
 works however the game ends.
Issue: https://github.com/GigiFrack/NX2Apple (fork)

---
 dm/gfx/nvn/hle_nvn.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dm/gfx/nvn/hle_nvn.c b/dm/gfx/nvn/hle_nvn.c
index 18a57a1..ea9f418 100644
--- a/dm/gfx/nvn/hle_nvn.c
+++ b/dm/gfx/nvn/hle_nvn.c
@@ -2017,6 +2017,9 @@ static void dump_frame(void) {
 counts_done:
     // Every 300 frames read resident memory and hand it to the graphics layer to print the memory readout line (mtl_mem_stat, low frequency, capped). Memory watchdog: when resident memory exceeds the cap, log a failure and exit on its own. On by default only on the Mac host (24 GB: runaway host memory
     // drags the whole machine into a kernel panic, which happened twice with other programs on the same machine), or set for tests with DM_MEM_CAP_GB=<integer>; the player's iOS app has no cap (exiting before the system kills it is pointless and only adds another kind of crash)
+    // DM_HLECOUNT: the table was written only on the way out, and a swipe from the app switcher kills the process before
+    // atexit runs, so the file never appeared. Write it with the rest of the 300-frame readouts instead.
+    if (g_frame % 300 == 0) { void hlecount_flush(void); hlecount_flush(); }
     if (g_frame % 300 == 0) { task_vm_info_data_t vi; mach_msg_type_number_t cnt = TASK_VM_INFO_COUNT;
         if (task_info(mach_task_self(), TASK_VM_INFO, (task_info_t)&vi, &cnt) == KERN_SUCCESS) { unsigned long long mb = (unsigned long long)(vi.phys_footprint >> 20); void mtl_mem_stat(unsigned long long, unsigned long long); mtl_mem_stat(g_frame, mb);
             static long cap = -1; if (cap < 0) { const char *e = getenv("DM_MEM_CAP_GB"); cap = e ? atol(e) : DM_MEM_CAP_DEFAULT_GB; }
